4. Commercial License

4.1 Commercial Use is permitted only after the user has obtained a Commercial
    License from the Licensors and paid the License Fee.

4.2 The License Fee is EUR 14,000 (fourteen thousand euros), paid once per
    legal entity. Value added tax or other taxes are added where they apply.

4.3 The License Fee is divided in equal shares among all Beneficiaries, so
    each of the seven Beneficiaries receives EUR 2,000. Each share is paid
    directly to that Beneficiary, against its own invoice or payment request,
    within 30 days of receipt. No Beneficiary may collect another
    Beneficiary's share.

4.4 Once the License Fee has been paid in full, the licensee receives a
    perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use, copy
    and modify the Software for its own Commercial Use, including for
    services it provides to its customers. The licensee may not sell,
    sublicense or publish the Software or a modified version of it as a
    standalone product.

4.5 A Commercial License is granted only in writing (e-mail is sufficient)
    and requires the consent of all Licensors. The Licensors may agree in
    writing to a different fee for a particular licensee; the Beneficiaries'
    shares remain equal.

4.6 Requests for a Commercial License: open an issue in this repository or
    contact the repository owner (GitHub: yacube69).


